<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP iron ore output up in October.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP iron ore output up in October.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Tuesday that its Australian iron ore output was higher in the five months to October as a result of increased customer demand. Queensland coal output for October was higher due to a preparation shutdown at Goonyella in October 1995. It was also higher on a year to date basis, BHP said.</p>
<p>Production of coal in New South Wales was higher for October due to the start of full production from Mount Owen, it said.</p>
<p>However, BHP said Indonesian coal output was lower during October than for the same month last year due to washout maintenance.  </p>
<p>BHP Minerals division output (million tonnes unless stated)</p>
<p>     Coal			     Oct 96  Oct 95   5-mths  yr ago</p>
<p>     - Australia (Qld)	     2.13    1.76    9.65    8.92</p>
<p>     - Australia (NSW)	     0.74    0.68    2.74    3.05</p>
<p>     - Indonesia		     0.42    0.54    2.45    2.19</p>
<p>     - USA			     1.03    1.09    5.40    5.48</p>
<p>    TOTAL				4.32    4.07   20.23   19.64</p>
<p>     Iron Ore (W.Australia)	4.62    4.43   22.82   20.71</p>
<p>     Iron Ore (Brazil)	     0.39    0.39    2.01    1.96</p>
<p>     Manganese ore (Australia)   0.20    0.20    0.84    0.82</p>
<p>     Ferro Alloys  (Australia)   0.02    0.02    0.09    0.09</p>
<p>Gold (fine ounces)</p>
<p>     - Mali			   3,360  11,411  52,217  49,237</p>
<p>Shipments</p>
<p>     - Coal  (total)		 4.62    4.10   19.63   19.26</p>
<p>     - Iron Ore (W.Australia)    4.36    4.57   21.76   20.88</p>
<p>NOTE: October is the fifth month of BHP's financial year.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
